  This is around 3hrs work in HTML, CSS and JS (a half finished project, content is to be added later, this is the
  visual framework). When we have projects with 40+ members taking half a decade.... Its not my place to cause trouble
  (never stopped me though) but be realistic about this. Do we really have the right people in the right places? Is it
  really the best practice to have people with zero experience in making apps deciding ALL decisions about how apps are
  made and designed (which is exactly what happens in practice)? Is it right to have the experts at the bottom and those
  with vastly less experience and talent above them dictating? I think its crystal clear to see that Link doesn't stand
  on its own and AI (Gemini) agrees "The user base of the Rakuten Link app closely mirrors the subscriber count of
  Rakuten Mobile, because activation and use of the app are heavily tied to the Rakuten Saikyo Plan". Exactly. Who
  believes that anyone would use Link if that tie was cut? And if subscribers would plumet, why? People use other apps
  without holding their phone plans value hostage, so why does Link need it?... Easy answer, its terrible. Users need to
  be forced to use it, else they would rather not.
  <br /><br />
  Gemini again: "If using the Rakuten Link app had no effect on the Rakuten Saikyo Plan—meaning it no longer offered the
  primary benefit of free unlimited domestic calls and SMS—the app's usage numbers would likely plummet drastically." Is
  that what we are working for? Or should we aim for better? Right now all I ever get told is to do the minimum and make
  tickets go away as quickly and as dirty as possible.
